# Target statements and their registry change only with the maintainer's approval
# (docs/design/Computation.md, F12, Q3). With branch protection on `main` requiring a code-owner
# review (a repository setting the maintainer turns on), no change to these paths merges without
# him. scripts/Targets.lean also fails on any branch where docs/targets.toml differs from the
# SHA-256 in docs/targets.approved.
#
# The handle @tchen01 is a guess from the maintainer's repository account and has not been
# confirmed by him yet (docs/port/status.md, open maintainer items); it is one replace-all here.
/docs/targets.toml @tchen01
/docs/targets.approved @tchen01
/NLAlib/**/*Targets.lean @tchen01
/.github/CODEOWNERS @tchen01
# The checks the guarantees rest on (final audits, 2026-10-24): the target lint, the axiom audit,
# the program checks, the kernel replay, the stage check and CI, and the build's pins (toolchain,
# Lake configuration and manifest), whose SHA-256 the registry records.
/scripts/Targets.lean @tchen01
/scripts/Audit.lean @tchen01
/scripts/Programs.lean @tchen01
/scripts/Replay.lean @tchen01
/scripts/stage_check.sh @tchen01
/.github/workflows/ @tchen01
/lakefile.toml @tchen01
/lake-manifest.json @tchen01
/lean-toolchain @tchen01
